# MSP Growth OS - API Test Suite
# Use VSCode REST Client extension to test these endpoints
# Set the variables below with your actual values

# For local testing, use:
@LOCAL_API = http://localhost:3000

# For AWS testing, use:
@API = https://your-api-gateway-url.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/prod

# Uncomment the one you want to use:
@BASE_URL = {{LOCAL_API}}
# @BASE_URL = {{API}}

@ACTION_ID = your-action-id-here

### 1. Initialize Data Catalog - Create Athena Views
# This creates the required views: scope_usage_vw, shelfware_vw, underbilling_vw
# Note: This will only work on AWS (requires Athena). Local version may fail gracefully.
POST {{BASE_URL}}/admin/bootstrap
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Get Actions Ledger for Specific Client
# Returns actions for a specific client (replace 'C001' with actual client_id)
GET {{BASE_URL}}/ledger?client_id=C001
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 3. Get All Actions Ledger
# Returns last 50 actions across all clients
GET {{BASE_URL}}/ledger
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 4. Get Shelfware Report
# Returns top 20 reclaimable seats by annual saving
GET {{BASE_URL}}/reports/shelfware
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 5. Get Underbilling Report  
# Returns invoice variance analysis with suggested addendums
GET {{BASE_URL}}/reports/underbilling
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6. Approve Action (Basic)
# Approve an action with default estimated savings
POST {{BASE_URL}}/actions/{{ACTION_ID}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

###

### 7. Approve Action with Custom Savings Override
# Approve an action with custom estimated savings amount
POST {{BASE_URL}}/actions/{{ACTION_ID}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "est_saving_inr": 50000,
  "send_email": false
}

###

### 8. Approve Action with Email (SES Sandbox)
# Approve and attempt to send email (requires verified sender/recipient in SES)
POST {{BASE_URL}}/actions/{{ACTION_ID}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "est_saving_inr": 75000,
  "send_email": true,
  "email_to": "customer@example.com"
}

###

### 9. Generate QBR PDF Report
# Generate PDF for specific client and period (replace with actual values)
POST {{BASE_URL}}/qbr/pdf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "C001",
  "period": "2025-09"
}

###

### 10. Evaluate Policies (Local Testing Only)
# Manually trigger policy evaluation (on AWS, this runs automatically via EventBridge)
POST {{BASE_URL}}/policies/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json

{
}

###

# Example Test Data Setup Commands:
# 
# 1. First, get your API URL from CDK deployment outputs:
#    aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name MspGrowthAppStack --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs'
#
# 2. Update the @API variable above with your actual API Gateway URL
#
# 3. To get an ACTION_ID for testing:
#    - Run the shelfware or underbilling report to see if there are any actions
#    - Or trigger the policy evaluator to create a PENDING action
#    - Or check the actions ledger to find an existing action_id
#
# 4. Replace 'acme' with actual client IDs from your data (e.g., 'C001', 'C002', etc.)
#
# 5. Adjust the period format to match your data (YYYY-MM format)

### Example Response Formats:
#
# Bootstrap Response:
# { "status": "ok" }
#
# Shelfware Response:
# {
#   "items": [
#     {
#       "client_id": "C001",
#       "app": "Office365",
#       "reclaimable_seats": "45",
#       "annual_saving_inr": "648000"
#     }
#   ]
# }
#
# Underbilling Response:
# {
#   "items": [
#     {
#       "client_id": "C001",
#       "period": "2024-01",
#       "hours": "120",
#       "expected_inr": "264000",
#       "billed_inr": "200000",
#       "delta_inr": "64000",
#       "suggestion": "Addendum: Invoice delta INR 64000 for 2024-01"
#     }
#   ]
# }
#
# Ledger Response:
# {
#   "items": [
#     {
#       "action_id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
#       "client_id": "C001",
#       "category": "how-to",
#       "status": "PENDING",
#       "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
#       "est_saving_inr": 10000
#     }
#   ]
# }
#
# Approve Response:
# {
#   "status": "APPROVED",
#   "action_id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
#   "email": {
#     "subject": "Action required: Approve change order (how-to)",
#     "body": "Dear customer,\n\nWe detected 4h over the contracted 10h..."
#   }
# }
#
# QBR PDF Response:
# {
#   "signedUrl": "https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucket/pdf/C001-2025-09.pdf?X-Amz-Algorithm=..."
# }
